It's pretty simple mate, the default behaviour is people get bearish when the price goes down and too bullish when it goes up.

I'm the opposite.

Bitcoin in the 60ks is considerably better value than it was at higher prices.

The old buy low sell high trick (it's a trick because most people cannot emotionally do it, and instead do the opposite).

@btcquokka @ZigIm_ @JoeConsorti @therationalroot @benjamincowen @jasonpizzino You're projecting, not expressing and opinion.

@scousehodl @btcquokka @JoeConsorti @therationalroot @benjamincowen @jasonpizzino Thank you.

I don't think I have ever used the term supercycle in a sentence to describe my views of Bitcoin (in fact I rip on that idea often).

I was one of the few people talking about the generational sell-side in 2025.

I have always said that we will only have confirmation that the bottom is in many months after it is in. Nobody knows on the day.

What I also say is that bottoms are a process and people will do much better if they stop trying to time THE bottom and just accumulate when it is cheap and hammering out the bottom (which is a multi-month and very painful process).

I still believe that bottom formation in this range is a likely scenario, and that that process started in February.

I also cannot predict the future and I say this almost every piece of analysis content I produce.

Remind me, what is your problem with me again?

